  "page1": {
    "title": "Stronger Together",
    "subtitle": "One ant is small, but a team can move a big leaf.",
    "body": "Look at one small ant on the ground. One ant cannot move a big leaf. But many ants can do it together. They push and pull as one team. This is the power of <u>cooperation</u>.\n\nPeople are very much the same. We live in a <mark>community</mark> with others. No one can do every job alone. Some people grow food on a farm. Some build homes, and some teach kids. Each person has a part to play.\n\nWhen we share work, the work gets easy. We must also take care of our own duty. A good member always keeps a promise. Together we are stronger than one. So let us help each other a little every day.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/14.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Many ants carry one big leaf together — one team, one goal."
  },
